From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: shell32: Open with

David: "a right click Open with option in the file manager is important."
SHOpenWithDialog and OpenAs_RunDLL were stubs, and the shell's menus had no
Open with. A file's menu (File Explorer, the desktop) now has "Open with..."
after its own verbs (not for programs or shortcuts), and the dialog is the
one Windows 10 shows: "How do you want to open this file?" -- the app that
opens the type now ("Keep using this app"), the others registered for it
(OpenWithProgids, OpenWithList, Applications whose SupportedTypes list it),
More apps (every application that opens files), and "Look for another app
on this PC" (registered for the user as Applications\name.exe). Apps are
named by their FriendlyAppName or version description. "Always use this app
to open .ext files" writes the user's choice (FileExts\.ext\UserChoice),
which ShellExecute follows.

Gate: make test-openwith.
